<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48629" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηλάζω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		aor. 1
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐθήλαξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					3.16
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αζε</span>
			): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηλή</span>): </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of the mother or nurse, <i>suckle</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Phryn.Com.
				29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				1.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				576b10
			</span></i>: abs., <i>give suck</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ μαστοί, οἳ οὐκ ἐθήλασαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
					23.29
				</span></i>
			:—also in 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιμελεῖσθαι, ὅπως μέτριον χρόνον
					θηλάσονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					460d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				566b17
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ συλλαμβάνουσι θηλαζόμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>GA</u>
					777a13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(2).514.12
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Lycosura</span>):—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be sucked</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ δελφὶς . . θηλάζεται ὑπὸ τῶν τέκνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					504b25
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of the young
			animal, <i>suck</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>GA</u>
				733b29
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλέφαντος ὁ σκύμνος θ. τῷ στόματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HA</u>
					578a22
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηλάζων χοῖρος</span> a
				<i>sucking</i> pig, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				14.15
			</span></i>; seldom of an infant, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				49.87
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεαίνας μασδὸν ἐθήλαξεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					3.16
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐὰν μὴ τύχῃ τεθηλακὼς ὁ ὄνος
					ἵππον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					577b16
				</span></i>
			. (Written 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θελάσζ-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PSI</u>
					4.368.19
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>.)</div>
